# The per-Dockerfile ignore for Dockerfile.toolchain (BuildKit rule: a
# `<Dockerfile-name>.dockerignore` beside the file OVERRIDES the root
# .dockerignore for builds with -f Dockerfile.toolchain). The root file
# is `*`-exclusive — it starves every root-context build to the release
# pipeline's staged `tmp/docker-context`, which is right for the server
# image but starves the toolchain cook (the first live cook, 2026-11-10:
# every COPY failed on "not found"). The toolchain image IS the repo's
# own build: allow the tree, minus the heavyweight and machine-local
# directories no cook reads.
.git
target
tmp
node_modules
dist
.fabro/cook
.fabro/judgments
